{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"goal","x":-700,"y":-1400,"width":1500,"height":340,"type":"text","text":"# Baseball Mechanics AI — 12-Month Roadmap\n**v1.0 · Aug 2026 – Jul 2027 · 2 people (US/Korea), ~50 hrs/wk combined**\n\n## Goal\nSingle-camera phone app that turns batting/pitching clips into body-mechanics data and coaching feedback — affordable for a high-school athlete with no hardware, no facility, no wearable.\n\n## The 12-Month Strategic Call\n**Ship batting only, to real users, with numbers you can defend.** Pitching = validated technical spike, not a shipped product. Golf/tennis = architected for, NOT built.\n\nThe canvas vision (4 sports × 3 platforms) is the right 5-year vision and the wrong 12-month plan. Ship one sport extremely well so sport #2 costs 30% of sport #1. That compounding is the actual asset.","color":"4"},
		{"id":"success","x":-1500,"y":-1000,"width":720,"height":340,"type":"text","text":"## Definition of Success (Month 12)\n\n| Outcome | Measured by |\n|---|---|\n| Real athletes using it | 50+ athletes, 500+ swings, ≥40% return |\n| Defensible numbers | Contact MAE < 15 ms; validated vs OpenBiomechanics |\n| Cited, not hallucinated | 100% claims → metric ID + timestamp; 0 banned claims |\n| Survivable economics | < $0.15 per analyzed swing |\n| Sport #2 is cheap | Pitching **spike** validated offline; ≥70% reuse |\n| **Can't silently break** | Stage regression tests green in CI |","color":"4"},
		{"id":"principle","x":-700,"y":-1000,"width":700,"height":340,"type":"text","text":"## ⚠️ The Non-Negotiable Principle\n\n> **Deterministic CV and geometry produce the measurements.**\n> **The language model reviews, explains, and coaches.**\n> **The language model NEVER produces a number.**\n\nThe moment an LLM estimates bat speed from pixels, the product becomes unfalsifiable, un-reproducible, and — with minors — indefensible.\n\nThis is policy, not a technical preference.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"state","x":80,"y":-1000,"width":720,"height":340,"type":"text","text":"## Where You Actually Are (Aug 2026)\n\n✅ **2D biomechanics overlay — the ONE stage working end to end**\n✅ Local batch pipeline (183 clips, memory-bounded)\n🟡 Pose extraction — **partial**, not reliable enough to build on\n🟡 Corpus: 173 Penn Action + 10 pro clips\n❌ **Batter selection + segmentation — NOT WORKING**\n❌ **2D→3D lifting (MotionBERT) — NOT WORKING**\n❌ **Event detection — never built**\n⏸ Bat tracking — failing (17% at contact) → **CUT from 12mo**\n❌ Capture gate · Feedback engine as code · App · Pitching\n\n**~25-30% through measurement, 0% through product.**\n**Q1 is a RECOVERY quarter, not an extension quarter.**","color":"3"},
		{"id":"physics","x":-1500,"y":-600,"width":720,"height":480,"type":"text","text":"## 🔬 Physics Limits — Design Around These\n\n| Constraint | Product response |\n|---|---|\n| 30fps = 33.3ms/frame; 70–90mph bat moves **1.0–1.34 m between frames** | Gate rejects 30fps for contact metrics |\n| 120fps → 0.26–0.34 m/fr; 240fps → 0.13–0.17 m/fr | 120fps min, 240fps recommended |\n| Monocular 3D: ambiguous scale + depth | Angles confident; distances gated behind calibration |\n| 2D wrist path ≠ 3D bat attack angle | Rename UI → \"hand-path angle (proxy)\" |\n| Exit velocity needs ball + time + scale | **Do not ship in Year 1. Say so.** |\n\n**Highest-leverage non-code action:** a capture protocol that gets users shooting 120fps+ on a tripod. Better input beats better model, costs nothing, can't be copied.","color":"6"},
		{"id":"audio","x":-700,"y":-600,"width":700,"height":480,"type":"text","text":"## 🎧 Audio Is Underrated\n\nBat-ball contact makes a sharp audio transient. A phone mic captures at **44.1 kHz** — roughly **1,470× the temporal resolution of a 30fps video frame**.\n\nAudio won't tell you *where* contact happened. It pins *when* to within a millisecond.\n\nFor a project whose central weakness is contact timing, this is the **cheapest accuracy win available**.\n\n→ Prototype in Q1 alongside the visual event model (M1.5).\n\n---\n\n## 🚫 Explicitly NOT in 12 Months\n❌ Golf / tennis  ❌ 3 platforms at once\n❌ Exit velocity / bat speed (physics)\n❌ Injury-risk claims (no truth, minors)\n❌ Pose training from scratch\n❌ Real-time on-device  ❌ Multi-camera","color":"6"},
		{"id":"agents","x":80,"y":-600,"width":720,"height":480,"type":"text","text":"## 🤖 AI Architecture — The Boundary\n\n```\nDETERMINISTIC LAYER — produces every number\ngate → pose → track → events → 3D → metrics\n        ↓ Evidence Packet (JSON, validated)\n   numbers cross this line ONE WAY\n        ↓\nREASONING LAYER — explains, never measures\nMEDA → APA → APE, backed by local VLM\n   every claim cites an evidence_id\n```\n\n**Two-lane local VLM (M5 Max, 128GB):**\n- **Fast** — Gemma 4 12B QAT Q4_0 (~6.98GB): capture QA, keyframes, drafts\n- **Strong** — Qwen3.6-35B-A3B 4bit (~20.4GB): escalation only\n\n**Escalation should be < 20% of runs.** Above that, fix the deterministic layer — not the model size.","color":"5"},
		{"id":"batting","x":-1500,"y":-60,"width":720,"height":720,"type":"text","text":"## 🏏 Technical Requirements — BATTING\n\n### Archetypes (drives baseline comparison)\n- **Power** — Judge, Ohtani, Raleigh, Schwarber, Alvarez\n- **Contact** — Lee Jung-hoo, Ichiro, Arraez, Hoerner\n- **Gap** — Olson, Devers, Freeman, Soto, Rafaela\n\nComparing a contact hitter to a power baseline = confidently wrong advice. Archetype is a **required** input.\n\n### User Inputs\narchetype · height/weight · handedness · video\n\n### Pipeline\n1. **Capture gate** — 8 dimensions, reject before inference `Q1`\n2. **Pose** — YOLO26m; COCO-17 insufficient → whole-body `Q2`\n3. **Player isolation** — mask + identity score (not ByteTrack ID alone) `Q1`\n4. **Keypoint quality** — tag `observed`/`interpolated`/`proxy`, never blend `Q1`\n5. **⭐ EVENT DETECTION** — 8 states: address→load→stride→foot plant→launch→**contact**→extension→finish `Q1`\n6. **3D lifting** — MotionBERT behind swappable adapter `Q1`\n7. **Metrics** — hip-shoulder sep, spine tilt, front-knee, lead-arm ext, hand-path proxy, time to contact `Q2`\n8. **Bat tracking** — TrackNet knob+tip, 200–500 labeled frames `Q3 conditional`\n9. **BLOCKED** — bat speed (scale), exit velo (ball) → Year 2","color":"2"},
		{"id":"pitching","x":-700,"y":-60,"width":700,"height":720,"type":"text","text":"## ⚾ Technical Requirements — PITCHING\n\n### Arm Slots (auto-classify, user-confirm)\n- **Overhand** — Schlittler, Cole, Yesavage, Miller\n- **Three-quarter** — Ohtani, Woo, Castillo, Yamamoto\n- **Sidearm** · **Underhand/submarine**\n\nMost amateurs misreport their own slot → classify from video.\n\n### Kinetic Chain\nground → legs → pelvis → trunk → shoulder → elbow → hand → release\n\nPitching is about **sequencing and timing**, not static positions. Never \"is the elbow right\" — always \"did the pelvis rotate before the trunk, by how many ms.\"\n\n### 9 Events\nfirst movement · peak leg lift · hand separation · max stride · **lead-foot contact** · **MER** · **ball release** · max lead-knee ext · finish\n\n⚠️ **MER** — few ms, severe blur. Below 240fps = unmeasurable.\n⚠️ **Ball release** — needs ball detection or very high fps.\n\n### Multi-Pitch Requirement\n**Minimum 5 pitches/session.** Report variance, not mean. Release *consistency* is the deliverable; release point is only an input. A single-pitch report is professionally misleading.\n\n### 🛑 Safety Policy — Decide Before Coding\n**Never output injury risk, prediction, or medical language.** Not as a hedge, not a %, not a \"flag.\" No ground truth exists; users are children. Enforce via banned-phrase validator in the schema — not a guideline someone must remember.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"shared","x":80,"y":-60,"width":720,"height":720,"type":"text","text":"## ♻️ The Reuse Thesis (= the multi-sport business case)\n\n| Reusable ~70% | Sport-specific ~30% |\n|---|---|\n| Capture quality gate | Event state model |\n| Pose extraction + tracking | Metric definitions |\n| Player isolation + identity | Archetype taxonomy |\n| 3D lifting adapter | Baseline library |\n| Evidence Packet schema | Coaching rubric |\n| MEDA/APA/APE engine | Capture protocol |\n| App shell, auth, storage, billing | — |\n\nGolf and tennis are structurally just **\"new event model + new metrics + new baseline library\"** on an existing spine.\n\nProve it with pitching in Q4 → the expansion story becomes credible to a partner, an investor, or a hire.\n\n---\n\n## 📦 Evidence Packet — The Key Interface\n\nEverything the reasoning layer sees, it sees through this. Nothing else.\n\n**Rules:**\n1. Not in the packet → agent can't discuss it. Kills most hallucination.\n2. Every metric carries a **CI**. Wide CI → soften or abstain.\n3. `baseline_comparison` computed by **retrieval**, not by the LLM.\n4. Schema-validate in AND out. 2 retries → abstain.\n\n**An honest abstention is a feature.** It's also the cheapest possible response.","color":"5"},
		{"id":"meda","x":-1500,"y":720,"width":720,"height":520,"type":"text","text":"## 🧠 MEDA → APA → APE as Running Code\n\nToday: conceptual roles. Make them **services with typed contracts.**\n\n**MEDA — target definition**\nIn: athlete profile → Out: target envelope + rationale\n⚠️ **Mostly RETRIEVAL, not generation.** Query the versioned baseline library. LLM writes prose *around* retrieved numbers — never invents them.\n\n**APA — current state**\nIn: Evidence Packet → Out: pros/cons by category, citing metric IDs\nDeterministic comparison first, LLM narrates second.\n\n**APE — recommendations**\nIn: MEDA target + APA gaps → Out: ranked, athlete-specific corrections + drills\nMust state *why* each correction follows from **this** athlete's gap. **Generic advice = failed run.**\n\n**Guardrails in code:** `evidence_id` required on every claim · banned-claim list checked post-generation · abstain path below confidence threshold","color":"5"},
		{"id":"baseline","x":-700,"y":720,"width":700,"height":520,"type":"text","text":"## 📚 Baseline Reference Library\n\nThe canvas promises feedback derived from professional samples. Implement as a **versioned metric distribution store** — NOT video similarity search.\n\n```\nbaseline_library/v1.2/\n  batting/\n    power_HS.json     # p10/p25/p50/p75/p90\n    contact_HS.json   # + n, source, capture cond.\n    gap_HS.json\n    power_pro.json    # aspirational tier\n  pitching/\n    overhand_HS.json\n    three_quarter_HS.json\n```\n\nComparison = **percentile lookup**. Fast, explainable, testable, versioned — so a baseline change never silently rewrites past reports.\n\n**Store cohort `n` and surface it.** A cohort of 6 must not be presented with the authority of a cohort of 300.","color":"5"},
		{"id":"data","x":80,"y":720,"width":720,"height":520,"type":"text","text":"## 🎥 Video Collection — 3 Distinct Needs\n\nConflating these is a common, expensive mistake.\n\n| Need | Purpose | Volume | Bar |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **A. Training** | fine-tune models | 1000s frames | messy, varied |\n| **B. Ground truth** | validate accuracy | 100s trials | lab-grade |\n| **C. Baselines** | cohort comparison | 30+/cohort | consistent protocol |\n\n### ⭐ Tier 1 — Driveline OpenBiomechanics\n**100 pitchers + 98 hitters.** C3D marker data: 47 body markers **+ 10 bat markers**. Free for educational use **through 31 Dec 2030**.\n\n**This is your ground truth (Need B) — the single most valuable external asset available. Download Week 1.** You currently have none.\n\n### Also\n**Penn Action** — 173 baseball_swing already extracted (7,561 frames). Good for robustness; ~30fps so useless for contact metrics.\n**MLB-YouTube** · **SportsPose / AthleticsPose**","color":"3"},
		{"id":"q1","x":-1500,"y":1300,"width":720,"height":540,"type":"text","text":"## 📅 Q1 · Aug–Oct 2026\n# ⚠️ \"RESTORE THE FOUNDATION\"\n**Recovery quarter.** 3 broken stages must work before anything new sits on them. **Do these IN ORDER.**\n\n| # | Deliverable | Own |\n|---|---|---|\n| M1.0 | **Regression harness FIRST** — why drift went unnoticed | FT |\n| M1.1 | **Batter selection + segmentation restored** — check if wrongly coupled to bat detection (may be same-day) | FT |\n| M1.2 | Pose reliability profile — where/why it fails | FT |\n| M1.3 | **3D lifting restored — 3-WEEK TIMEBOX** | FT |\n| M1.4 | OpenBiomechanics loaded (ground truth) | PT |\n| M1.5 | Capture protocol + consent form | PT |\n| M1.6 | Golden set: 200–500 swings labeled | PT |\n| M1.7 | Capture quality gate | FT |\n| M1.9 | Event detection **STARTED** (finishes Q2) | FT |\n\n### 🔀 FALLBACK if 3D won't restore in 3 weeks\n**Ship 2D-only.** Your 2D overlay works today. Separation, spine tilt, front-knee are coachable from 2D with a view-dependence caveat. 3D → Q3 upgrade. **Don't let a broken stage hold the year hostage.**","color":"1"},
		{"id":"q2","x":-700,"y":1300,"width":700,"height":540,"type":"text","text":"## 📅 Q2 · Nov 2026–Jan 2027\n# \"TRUSTWORTHY FEEDBACK\"\nFinish event detection, then turn numbers into coaching.\n\n| # | Deliverable | Own |\n|---|---|---|\n| M2.0 | **⭐ EVENT DETECTION SHIPPED — MAE < 15ms** *(carried from Q1)* | FT |\n| M2.1 | Evidence Packet v1 + validator | FT |\n| M2.2 | Baseline library v1 (3 archetypes) | PT |\n| M2.3 | Gemma fast lane live locally | FT |\n| M2.4 | MEDA/APA/APE as services | FT |\n| M2.5 | Validation report vs OpenBiomechanics; kill unsupportable claims | Both |\n| M2.6 | **⭐ CLOSED ALPHA — 10 athletes** | Both |\n| M2.7 | Cost instrumentation from day 1 | FT |\n\n### 🚦 EXIT GATE\n- **Contact MAE < 15 ms @ 240fps**\n- 10 athletes received reports\n- **≥7 rate feedback \"specific and useful\"**\n- 100% claims carry evidence citation · **0 banned claims**","color":"1"},
		{"id":"q3","x":80,"y":1300,"width":720,"height":540,"type":"text","text":"## 📅 Q3 · Feb–Apr 2027\n# \"MAKE IT A PRODUCT\"\nApp, scale, retention.\n\n| # | Deliverable | Own |\n|---|---|---|\n| M3.1 | **PICK ONE PLATFORM** → rec: mobile web/PWA (no store review, instant iteration) | Both |\n| M3.2 | App v1: upload→gate→results→overlay | FT |\n| M3.3 | FastAPI + S3 + auth + consent | FT |\n| M3.4 | **Progress tracking = #1 retention driver** | PT |\n| M3.5 | Baseline lib v2 (30+/cohort, pro tier) | PT |\n| M3.6 | 3D lifting — **if deferred from Q1**, restore as accuracy upgrade | FT |\n| M3.7 | ❌ **Bat tracking CUT from 12-month plan** → Year 2 | — |\n| M3.8 | **⭐ OPEN BETA — 50+ athletes** | Both |\n\n### 🚦 EXIT GATE\n- 50 athletes onboarded\n- **≥40% return for a 2nd session**\n- Cost/swing < $0.15 · p95 turnaround < 5 min","color":"1"},
		{"id":"q4","x":880,"y":1300,"width":720,"height":540,"type":"text","text":"## 📅 Q4 · May–Jul 2027\n# ⚠️ \"HARDEN BATTING, SPIKE PITCHING\"\n**Revised:** pitching *alpha* CUT → offline *spike*. A recovery quarter was absorbed; shipping sport #2 now means shipping both badly.\n\n| # | Deliverable | Own |\n|---|---|---|\n| M4.1 | **BATTING HARDENING — the priority.** Reliability, turnaround, cost, retention | FT |\n| M4.2 | Pitching spike: 9-event model + arm-slot classifier, **validated offline vs OpenBiomechanics. NO USERS.** | FT |\n| M4.3 | Safety validator built before any pitching output is shown | Both |\n| M4.4 | Pitching baselines (overhand, 3/4) | PT |\n| M4.5 | **Reuse report + golf/tennis cost model** | Both |\n| M4.6 | Year-2 plan — on evidence, not the vision doc | Both |\n\n### 🚦 EXIT GATE\n- Batting stable, **≥40% retention holding at scale**\n- Pitching spike validated offline\n- **≥70% reuse proven — without a 2nd launch**\n\n**Why cut the alpha?** 50 weekly batting users is a real asset. A 10-user pitching alpha + shaky batting is neither.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"limits","x":-1500,"y":1900,"width":720,"height":700,"type":"text","text":"## ⚠️ Limitations — 2 People, 2 Continents\n\n| Constraint | Real consequence |\n|---|---|\n| ~50 hrs/wk combined | 1 major + 1 support workstream. Not 4 sports. |\n| **13–14 hr time gap** | Near-zero overlap. Live debugging together = 1 day lost per exchange. |\n| 2 people = 2 bus factors of 1 | Illness/job change/burnout stops the project outright |\n| No specialist depth | Some problems take 3× a specialist's time |\n| No ground-truth hardware | No force plate, mocap, or radar → dependent on public data + partnerships |\n| Labeling is a hard floor | 300 swings ≈ 15–20 hrs of human work. Can't be automated away. |\n\n### Turning the gap into an advantage\n- **Split by ownership, never by task.** FT owns pipeline; PT owns data/labeling/baselines/recruiting. Interfaces = files and schemas, not conversations.\n- **Contracts before code.** Agree the JSON schema, then build independently. This is why the Evidence Packet matters *organizationally*.\n- **Async default** — written decisions (keep MEMORY.md current), recorded walkthroughs, PRs that assume the reader is asleep.\n- **One weekly sync, non-negotiable.** 60 min, agenda in advance, decisions logged.\n- **Korea cohort = generalization test,** not redundancy. Two baseball cultures in your training data is a real technical asset most 2-person teams can't claim.","color":"6"},
		{"id":"growth","x":-700,"y":1900,"width":700,"height":700,"type":"text","text":"## 📣 Growing the Team\n\n### Phase 1 (Q1–Q2) — Advisors, not employees\n- **1 biomechanics advisor** — college/HS strength coach or kinesiology grad student. Offer free analysis + co-authorship. **Highest-ROI relationship available:** validates metric definitions before you ship something a domain expert would reject on sight.\n- **2–3 coach design partners** — they tell you if feedback is actionable. No benchmark can.\n\n### Phase 2 (Q2–Q3) — Build in public\nRecruiting follows attention; attention follows artifacts.\n- Publish the validation work — *\"our contact-detection error vs marker-based mocap\"* reaches CV engineers who care\n- Open-source something useful but non-core (capture gate, Penn Action labeling tools). Signals competence, costs no moat.\n- Present at SABR / SSAC — the baseball analytics community is unusually open and actively looks for this\n- **Korea advantage:** large market, underserved by English tools, partner already positioned. Korean-language product = real differentiation, not translation.\n\n### Phase 3 (Q3–Q4) — Targeted contributors\n| Gap | Who | Engagement |\n|---|---|---|\n| Labeling | Sports-science students | Paid hourly / credit |\n| Mobile | Contract PWA dev | Fixed scope, 4–6 wks |\n| Biomech validation | Kinesiology grad | Research collab |\n| Data | Facility owner | Data-for-analysis trade |\n\n**What makes people join a 2-person project:** a working demo, a scoped problem, evidence you ship. You'll have #1 by Q2 and #3 by Q3. **Recruit then** — not now.","color":"6"},
		{"id":"risk","x":80,"y":1900,"width":720,"height":700,"type":"text","text":"## 🎲 Risk Register\n\n| # | Risk | L | I | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **R0** | **Broken stages take > Q1 to restore** | **H** | **CRIT** | Timebox each fix (3wk for 3D). **Take the 2D-only fallback rather than extending.** 2D overlay already works = shippable floor. |\n| **R0b** | **More silent regressions appear** | M | H | M1.0 regression harness is the first deliverable of the year — precisely because this already happened once |\n| R1 | Event detection misses 15ms | M | **CRIT** | Audio fusion as parallel path; if both fail ship non-contact metrics only (sep/tilt/knee stay valid) |\n| R2 | Users shoot 30fps anyway | **H** | H | Gate + in-app camera w/ fps enforcement; degrade gracefully, don't refuse |\n| R3 | Labeling bottleneck | H | M | Start Week 1; active learning; budget paid labelers Q3 |\n| R4 | One person unavailable | M | **CRIT** | Written decisions, no tribal knowledge, both can run full pipeline |\n| R5 | Metrics fail validation | M | H | Better learned early than post-launch. Narrowing claims **is a successful outcome.** |\n| R6 | Bat tracking eats the year | — | — | ✅ **Resolved — cut from the 12-month plan entirely** |\n| R7 | Scope creep → golf/tennis | **H** | H | The \"NOT doing\" list exists to be pointed at |\n| R8 | Youth data/privacy misstep | L | **CRIT** | Consent from Q1; minimize retention; never train on non-consented footage |","color":"6"},
		{"id":"four","x":-700,"y":2660,"width":1500,"height":380,"type":"text","text":"# 🎯 The Four Things That Matter Most\n*If everything else is noise, these are the load-bearing decisions.*\n\n### 1. Restore the pipeline before extending it — and make silent breakage impossible\nThree stages recorded as working are not. Regression harness first, then batter selection → pose → 3D lifting, in that order. Event detection is still the gate on every at-contact metric, but it can't be built on a foundation that doesn't hold.\n\n### 2. Never let the model produce a number\nThe deterministic/reasoning boundary is what makes this defensible. Protect it **in code**, not in convention.\n\n### 3. Ship one sport, one platform, to real users\nA batting product 50 athletes use weekly is worth vastly more than four half-built sports — as a business, a technical asset, and a recruiting story.\n\n### 4. Say what you cannot measure\nPhysics blocks exit velocity, bat speed, and true 3D attack angle from one uncalibrated phone. Competitors will overclaim. **Being the honest tool is a durable differentiator with coaches** — and coaches decide adoption.","color":"4"}
	],
